re taking the database course.\n\n5. **All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David.**\n   - This means that if a student works in the lab, they are instructed by professor David.\n\n6. **James is a student working in the lab.**\n   - This means that James works in the lab.\n\n7. **Jack neither has a part-time job offered by the university nor works in the lab.**\n   - This means that Jack does not have a part-time job and does not work in the lab.\n\nNow, let\'s analyze the statement "James either takes the database course or has a part-time job offered by the university."\n\n- Since James works in the lab, he is instructed by professor David (from step 4).\n- Since professor David instructs students taking the database course (from step 5), James must be taking the database course.\n- Therefore, James cannot have a part-time job offered by the university because he is already working in the library (from step 2).\n\nThus, the statement "James either takes the database course or has a part-time job offered by the university" is false because James is taking the database course and does not have a part-time job offered by the university.\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
