messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nNo students who work in the library are from the computer science department. All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library. All students who take the database course are from the computer science department. All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course. All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David. James is a student working in the lab. Jack neither has a part-time job offered by the university nor works in the lab.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? James does not have a part-time job offered by the university.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain. I think the correct option is: B\n', '<think>.\nTo determine if the statement "James does not have a part-time job offered by the university" is true, false, or uncertain, we need to analyze the given information step by step.\n\n1. **No students who work in the library are from the computer science department.**.\n   - This means that if a student works in the library, they cannot be from the computer science department.\n\n2. **All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library.**.\n   - This means that if a student has a part-time job offered by the university, they must be working in the library.\n\n3. **All students who take the database course are from the computer science department.**.\n   - This means that if a student takes the database course, they must be from the computer science department.\n\n4. **All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course.**.\n   - This means that if a student is instructed by professor David, they must be taking the database course.\n\n5. **All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David.**.\n   - This means that if a student is working in the lab, they must be instructed by professor David.\n\n6. **James is a student working in the lab.**.\n   - This means that James is working in the lab.\n\n7. **Jack neither has a part-time job offered by the university nor works in the lab.**.\n   - This means that Jack does not have a part-time job offered by the university and does not work in the lab.\n\nNow, let\'s analyze the information step by step:.\n\n- Since James is working in the lab, and all students working in the lab are instructed by professor David, James must be taking the database course.\n- Since all students taking the database course are from the computer science department, James must be from the computer science department.\n- Since no students who work in the library are from the computer science department, James cannot be working in the library.\n- Since all students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library, James cannot have a part-time job offered by the university.\n\nTherefore, based on the given information, the statement "James does not have a part-time job offered by the university" is true.\n\n<｜User｜>Please solve the logical reasoning problem. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
