naged building if and only if he is allowed to move in with Fluffy, and the security deposit is no more than $1500**: This condition states that Tom will rent an apartment in a managed building only if he is allowed to move in with his cat and the security deposit is no more than $1500.\n\nNow, let\'s analyze the information:.\n\n- Since Fluffy is Tom\'s cat and cats are pets, Tom is allowed to move in with Fluffy in a managed building.\n- The Olive Garden is a managed building where pets are allowed.\n- The monthly rent at the Olive Garden is $2000, which is more than $1500. Therefore, the security deposit cannot be $2000 or more, as it must be no more than $1500.\n\nGiven these points, Tom cannot rent an apartment in The Olive Garden because the security deposit requirement is not met. Thus, the statement "Tom will rent an apartment in The Olive Garden" is false.\n\n<｜User｜>Based on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Tom will rent an apartment in The Olive Garden.\n# Options:.\nA) True.\nB) False.\nC) Uncertain.\n<｜Assistant｜>. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
