rge has access to a program (\\( P \\)), then he can compose (\\( C \\)).\n   - However, we need to ensure that the combination \\( L \\land P \\) leads to \\( W \\).\n\n5. **Conclusion:**.\n   - Since \\( L \\rightarrow W \\) and \\( P \\rightarrow C \\), and combining these with the fact that \\( W \\land C \\rightarrow W \\), we can conclude that if George likes music and has access to a program, he will indeed want to compose.\n   - Therefore, the statement "If George likes music and has access to a program, he will compose" is true.\n\n<｜User｜>Based on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? If George likes music and has access to a program, he will compose.\n# Options:.\nA) True.\nB) False.\nC) Uncertain.\n<｜Assistant｜>.\nBased on the given information, the statement "If George likes music and has access to a program, he will compose" is true. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
