.\n- Since Ben is popular, he cannot be ugly (from point 2).\n- Since Ben is not ugly, he cannot be yellow (from point 5).\n\nIn both scenarios, Ben cannot be both ugly and yellow. Therefore, the statement "Ben is ugly or yellow" is false.\n\n<｜Assistant｜>\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
